── Benign companion a11y child (expected, not a regression) ────────────────
The live a11y dump shows ONE extra child node under each row's merged
Switch node this cycle (absent in cycle-3's dump): an empty
`android.view.View`, `content-desc=""`, `clickable="false"`,
`focusable="false"`. This matches — and is independently CONFIRMED live,
not just trusted from the unit test — the engineer's own documented
tradeoff in n_settings_tile.dart's inline comment and the updated
n_settings_tile_test.dart predicate (NModuleSwitcher precedent): a
`FocusableActionDetector` internally wraps `Shortcuts` -> its own
`Focus(includeSemantics: true)`, which `includeFocusSemantics: false` never
reaches — an SDK-internal artifact, not the InkWell-leak class of bug
NEARS-3701 fixed. It carries no label and no tap action on either row (live-
verified, both dumps above), so no assistive-technology user would ever
land on it as a meaningful stop — NEARS-3701's actual AC ("no second node
that absorbs the label or the tap action") still holds; only the raw node
COUNT changed, which the engineer's updated test correctly re-scoped to
content rather than a strict count. Not filed as a bug; noted here for the
record since a raw count-only re-check would have looked like a regression
without this context.

